Here are a couple of script files I just whipped up.  Take a look
at them - they are easy to use and can save you lots of time as they
do for me.  Feel free to expand on them as well (so far they allow
only 2 directories) but please let me know what you think of them.

     file 1:

     START

-----cut here-----
echo
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo %:::::::::::START will set up your AUTO FHUNT scripts.:::::::::::%
echo %::Proper syntax:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::%
echo %:::::START [abbrev] [ftp_address] [directory1] [directory2]:::::%
echo %::example:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::%
echo %:::::START cs cs.uwp.edu /pub/msdos/games /pub/msdos/games/temp %
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo

echo ftp $2 > $1
chmod ugo+x $1

mkdir _$1
cd _$1

echo > $1Res

echo anonymous > $1Script
echo cd $3    >> $1Script
echo dir      >> $1Script
echo cd $4    >> $1Script
echo dir      >> $1Script
echo quit     >> $1Script

cd ..
echo Setup is done.  To run AUTO FHUNT type:
echo     AUTO $1
echo
--------cut here------

     Here is the second file.  If you type (for example) "cs", you
     will be able to ftp to cs.uwp.edu.  But type "AUTO cs" to make
     use of the following program:

     file 2:

     AUTO

-------cut here------
echo
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo %::AUTO FHUNT - Automatic Ftp File Hunt program by Travis Emmitt::%
echo %:::Please type email address or x at Password prompt and then::::%
echo %::AUTO FHUNT will find all the new files since your last FHUNT:::%
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo %:::::::::::It might take a few seconds, so be patient::::::::::::%
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo

cd _$1
mv $1Res $1Old
../$1 < $1Script > $1Res
echo
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo % New files since last FHUNT: %
echo %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
echo

diff $1Res $1Old | grep '< '
cd ..
--------cut here-------

